 "drivingQuestion": "What are the antikei not sold with a ship?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "term glossed",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_batra.77b.4",
   "daf": "77b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "אֲבָל לֹא מָכַר לֹא אֶת הָעֲבָדִים וְלֹא אֶת הַמַּרְצוּפִין וְלֹא אֶת הָאַנְתִיקֵי וְכוּ׳. מַאי ״אַנְתִיקֵי״? אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: עִיסְקָא דִּבְגַוַּוהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that when one sells a ship he has sold various other items; «but he has not sold the slaves, nor the packing bags, nor the antikei.» But when one said to the buyer: You are purchasing the ship and all that it contains, all of these are sold as well. The Gemara asks: «What» is the meaning of «antikei? Rav Pappa said:» It means «the merchandise that is on» the ship. This merchandise is not sold together with the ship."
  }
 ],
